Z||000015||Max The Chainsaw||06-21-2001||12:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RossT:<BR><B>Whats the switch where the rear defog switch is normally?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's for the fog lights. Been contemplating trying to hook a relay into the neutral switch of the auto and hook to them as daytime running lights but I think that may be a bit "Ricey..." LOL<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Max The Chainsaw||06-21-2001||12:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Max The Chainsaw:<BR><B> That's for the fog lights. Been contemplating trying to hook a relay into the neutral switch of the auto and hook to them as daytime running lights but I think that may be a bit "Ricey..." LOL<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, and before anyone asks.... the switch on the back left side of the dash is hooked to the headlight switch white wire. I switch it up if I make a lot of stops at night or during winter snow and ice storms to keep the headlights open and save wear on the motors or keep em from being froze shut.<BR>||||reg||1
